EDITS = {'CHANGELOG.md': [('lines 1-1', '## [1.144.0] - a pack material samples its textures as the pack asks\n', '## [1.145.0] - a window has a frame and a sill\n\nThe factory\'s roadmap 324; the walker, 2026-10-28: "i think its less about realistic textures and more about the 3d\nshape themselves?", and of the plan that followed, "Yes now you get it". A window was a hole in a slab with a pane at\nmid-depth: on the bank\'s 30 cm wall a 13 cm reveal, in the wall\'s own material, which any light that lit the face lit\nthe same, so the window read as a dark square painted on the wall (seed 9082, the factory\'s\n`docs/findings/window_frames/`). Only an Empty\'s window had more, and from elsewhere: its sash is painted on the pane\n(`window_panes`) and its stone sill and lintel are Patina dressing.\n\n### Added\n- **A window\'s frame** (`arch.window_frame_parts`): stiles and rails ringing the opening on the pane\'s plane, a\n  mullion down a pane wider than 1.2 m, 5 cm wide, standing 12.5 mm proud of the pane on each face\n  (`window_frame_depth`: 7 cm in a 30 cm wall; derived from the pane, which is a fraction of the wall, because a fixed\n  7 cm was thinner than the pane on the genome\'s 0.6 m wall). In the storefront\'s painted aluminium. An open shell:\n  the faces on the slab and inside the frame are not built (`window_frame_dropped`). No collider.\n- **A window\'s sill** (`arch.window_sill_parts`): 5 cm tall, standing 1.5 cm on the slab\'s sill, from just inside the\n  frame to 5 cm past the outdoor face, bearing 5 cm into each jamb; none where the opening reaches the floor. In the\n  wall\'s own material, bevelled with the butt planes. No collider. It is outside the slot, so the module\'s fit leaves\n  it out (`fit_objects`, as a swung leaf is left out of a door\'s): fitted on everything, the first build of seed 9082\n  re-centred every framed window -- slab, collider and all -- 2.5 cm off its slot, a step in the facade at both ends\n  of the module, seen in its frames and kept in the factory\'s finding.\n- Neither on a painted pane (an Empty\'s, which carries its own) nor on a glass wall.\n\n### Measured\n- `tools/coplanar_census.py --species window`: 4 pairs at each corner, 12 in all -- the `RESIDUE` row, unchanged. The\n  first draft ran the sill back to the pane\'s plane and the census counted the pane\'s bottom edge 1.5 mm off the\n  sill\'s top; the sill now starts 5 mm inside the frame\'s face, and the frame\'s depth follows the pane.\n- 76 more triangles a window at the genome\'s corners (124 -> 200 at max).\n\nTests: tests/test_window_frame.py (fails on 1.144.0; its bpy half in Blender). The factory\'s\npatches/patch_zoo_window_frame.py, written by tools/ship_change.py.\n\n## [1.144.0] - a pack material samples its textures as the pack asks\n')], 'VERSION': [('lines 1-1', '1.144.0', '1.145.0')], 'zoo_keeper/core/arch.py': [('lines 748-749', '\ndef storefront_parts(w: float, d: float, h: float, void: dict | None = None,\n', '\n#: A FRAMED WINDOW (1.145.0). The walker, 2026-10-28, of what makes an asset read\n#: as real: "i think its less about realistic textures and more about the 3d shape\n#: themselves?". A window was a hole in a slab with a pane at mid-depth: a 13 cm\n#: reveal on a 30 cm wall, in the wall\'s own material, so under any light that\n#: lit the face it lit the reveal the same and the window read as a dark square\n#: painted on the wall (seed 9082\'s bank, the factory\'s\n#: `docs/findings/realism_trial/`). A window has a frame the glass is set in and\n#: a sill that throws a shadow line; those are what this builds.\n#:\n#: THE FRAME is a ring inside the opening, on the pane\'s plane, standing\n#: `WINDOW_FRAME_PROUD` proud of the pane on both faces (`window_frame_depth`:\n#: the pane is a fraction of the wall, so a fixed depth was thinner than the\n#: pane on the genome\'s 0.6 m wall), with a mullion down the middle of a\n#: pane wider than `WINDOW_MULLION_OVER`. An open shell like a casing: every\n#: face that lies on a jamb, the sill or the head, and a rail\'s ends inside a\n#: stile, is not built (`window_frame_dropped`), so nothing is coplanar. No\n#: collider: an opening\'s collision stays the slab\'s.\n#:\n#: THE SILL stands on the slab\'s sill, `WINDOW_SILL_LIFT` above it so its top is\n#: a face of its own, from `WINDOW_SILL_TUCK` inside the frame\'s outdoor face\n#: out past the wall\'s (+Y) by `WINDOW_SILL_PROUD`, bearing `WINDOW_SILL_BEAR`\n#: into each jamb. Outdoors only, and only where the slab has a sill to stand it\n#: on. Its underside past the face is the shadow line. Its back stops short of\n#: the pane: the first draft ran it to the pane\'s plane, and the census\n#: (`tools/coplanar_census.py --species window`) counted the pane\'s bottom edge\n#: 1.5 mm off the sill\'s top, a pair the slab never had.\n#:\n#: NOT on a painted pane: `window_panes` paints a rowhouse\'s sash, and the\n#: Empties that carry one get Patina\'s stone sill and lintel as dressing\n#: (`dressing.sill_parts`), so a second would stand in the first.\nWINDOW_FRAME_W = 0.05\nWINDOW_FRAME_PROUD = 0.0125\nWINDOW_MULLION_OVER = 1.2\nWINDOW_SILL_H = 0.05\nWINDOW_SILL_PROUD = 0.05\nWINDOW_SILL_BEAR = 0.05\nWINDOW_SILL_LIFT = 0.015\nWINDOW_SILL_TUCK = 0.005\n\n\ndef window_frame_depth(d: float) -> float:\n    """How deep a window\'s frame is in a wall ``d`` deep: the pane\'s\n    thickness (``d * SF_PANE_D``) and ``WINDOW_FRAME_PROUD`` either side, no\n    deeper than the wall -- 0.07 m in a 0.30 m wall."""\n    return min(d, d * SF_PANE_D + 2.0 * WINDOW_FRAME_PROUD)\n\n\ndef window_frame_parts(d: float, void: dict, width: float = WINDOW_FRAME_W):\n    """The frame of a window whose opening is ``void``, on the pane\'s plane\n    (``y = 0``): ``(name, (cx, cy, cz), (sx, sy, sz))`` boxes -- ``Frame_L`` /\n    ``Frame_R`` stiles the opening\'s full height, ``Frame_B`` / ``Frame_T``\n    rails between them, and ``Frame_M`` between the rails where the pane is\n    wider than ``WINDOW_MULLION_OVER``. No wider than a third of the opening\n    either way; ``window_frame_depth(d)`` deep."""\n    x0, x1, z0, z1 = void["x0"], void["x1"], void["z0"], void["z1"]\n    fw = min(width, (x1 - x0) / 3.0, (z1 - z0) / 3.0)\n    fd = window_frame_depth(d)\n    out = []\n\n    def box(name, bx0, bx1, bz0, bz1):\n        out.append((name, (round((bx0 + bx1) / 2.0, 6), 0.0, round((bz0 + bz1) / 2.0, 6)),\n                    (round(bx1 - bx0, 6), round(fd, 6), round(bz1 - bz0, 6))))\n\n    box("Frame_L", x0, x0 + fw, z0, z1)\n    box("Frame_R", x1 - fw, x1, z0, z1)\n    box("Frame_B", x0 + fw, x1 - fw, z0, z0 + fw)\n    box("Frame_T", x0 + fw, x1 - fw, z1 - fw, z1)\n    if x1 - x0 - 2.0 * fw > WINDOW_MULLION_OVER:\n        mid = (x0 + x1) / 2.0\n        box("Frame_M", mid - fw / 2.0, mid + fw / 2.0, z0 + fw, z1 - fw)\n    return out\n\n\ndef window_frame_dropped(name: str, normal) -> bool:\n    """Whether a face of frame box ``name`` with ``normal`` (x, y, z) lies on\n    the slab or inside another part of the frame: a stile\'s outer side and its\n    ends, a rail\'s outer side and its ends, a mullion\'s ends."""\n    nx, nz = normal[0], normal[2]\n    if name == "Frame_L":\n        return nx < -0.9 or abs(nz) > 0.9\n    if name == "Frame_R":\n        return nx > 0.9 or abs(nz) > 0.9\n    if name == "Frame_B":\n        return nz < -0.9 or abs(nx) > 0.9\n    if name == "Frame_T":\n        return nz > 0.9 or abs(nx) > 0.9\n    return abs(nz) > 0.9\n\n\ndef window_sill_parts(w: float, d: float, h: float, void: dict):\n    """The outdoor sill of a window ``w`` x ``d`` x ``h`` whose opening is\n    ``void``: one ``("Sill_Stone", centre, size)`` box, or ``[]`` where the\n    opening reaches the floor or the slab\'s sill is too short to stand it on.\n    It bears into the jambs no further than the jambs reach."""\n    hw, hh = w / 2.0, h / 2.0\n    x0, x1, z0 = void["x0"], void["x1"], void["z0"]\n    if z0 - (-hh) < WINDOW_SILL_H:\n        return []\n    bear = max(0.0, min(WINDOW_SILL_BEAR, x0 + hw, hw - x1))\n    top = z0 + WINDOW_SILL_LIFT\n    y0, y1 = window_frame_depth(d) / 2.0 - WINDOW_SILL_TUCK, d / 2.0 + WINDOW_SILL_PROUD\n    return [("Sill_Stone", (round((x0 + x1) / 2.0, 6), round((y0 + y1) / 2.0, 6),\n                            round(top - WINDOW_SILL_H / 2.0, 6)),\n             (round(x1 - x0 + 2.0 * bear, 6), round(y1 - y0, 6), WINDOW_SILL_H))]\n\n\ndef storefront_parts(w: float, d: float, h: float, void: dict | None = None,\n')], 'zoo_keeper/recipes/_arch.py': [('lines 51-52', '    objs, cboxes = [], []\n\n', "    objs, cboxes = [], []\n    proud = []          # parts standing out of the slot, left out of the fit (a window's sill)\n\n"), ('lines 284-285', '            objs.append(pane)\n\n', '            objs.append(pane)\n        # A FRAMED WINDOW (1.145.0, `arch.window_frame_parts`): the frame in the\n        # storefront\'s painted aluminium, the sill in the wall\'s own material, so\n        # it packs into the wall side\'s mesh. Not on a painted pane, which\n        # paints its sash and gets its sill as dressing; not on a glass wall.\n        if painted is None and plan["material"] not in arch.SF_FRAME_FOR:\n            frame = []\n            for name, center, size in arch.window_frame_parts(d, void):\n                bm = geometry.new_bm()\n                geometry.add_box(bm, center, size)\n                geometry.drop_faces(bm, lambda n, nm=name: arch.window_frame_dropped(nm, n))\n                frame.append(geometry.bm_to_object(\n                    bm, f"{root}_{name}", collection, bevel=0.0, texel=1.0,\n                    rng=rng, wear=wear * 0.5, smooth_angle=_WALL_SMOOTH))\n            materials.assign(frame, materials.make_material(\n                "M_Storefront_frame", list(arch.SF_FRAME_RGB), arch.SF_FRAME_KIND))\n            objs.extend(frame)\n            for name, center, size in arch.window_sill_parts(w, d, h, void):\n                bm = geometry.new_bm()\n                geometry.add_box(bm, center, size)\n                sill = geometry.bm_to_object(\n                    bm, f"{root}_{name}", collection, bevel=bevel, texel=1.0,\n                    rng=rng, wear=wear, smooth_angle=_WALL_SMOOTH, butt_planes=butts)\n                materials.assign([sill], structure)\n                objs.append(sill)\n                proud.append(sill)\n\n'), ('lines 340-340', '    return {"objects": objs, "collision_boxes": cboxes, "attachments": {}}\n', '    # A SILL IS OUTSIDE THE SLOT (1.145.0). It stands out of one face only, and\n    # `build._recentre` centres a module on what it fits: on everything, the\n    # first build moved each framed window -- slab, collider and all -- 2.5 cm\n    # off its slot, a step in the facade at both its ends. The fit is the rest,\n    # as a swung leaf is left out of a door\'s.\n    out = {"objects": objs, "collision_boxes": cboxes, "attachments": {}}\n    if proud:\n        out["fit_objects"] = [o for o in objs if o not in proud]\n    return out\n')]}
